// Now, there are definitely already some things that developers can do to avoid this, however
// all of them are not as clean as having a seperate brand new ReturnType for asynchronous functions.
// This is where the AsyncReturnType comes in. It is a utility type that 
// allows developers to get the return type of an asynchronous function.

// An example of usage could be a developer using Prisma and including many custom parameters in their returning data. 
// Prisma's types are autogenerated, and therefore the return type of the function would also be auto-generated, eliminating wasted development time.

// Here's the function.

